      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.61,
      "end_seconds": 5.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "doctor? Hello, I hope this is the right time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.22,
      "end_seconds": 12.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "So, yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.02,
      "end_seconds": 21.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Honestly, it's a fever, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.67,
      "end_seconds": 27.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.08,
      "end_seconds": 42.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Right, nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.41,
      "end_seconds": 73.07,
      "duration_seconds": 10.66,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 120 over 66, SpO2 97 percent on room air, temperature 39.1. And respiratory rate 17, heart rate 107."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.93,
      "end_seconds": 88.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.12,
      "end_seconds": 98.1,
      "duration_seconds": 7.98,
      "text": "It's been two days, I'm fairly sure. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.79,
      "end_seconds": 101.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.76,
      "end_seconds": 103.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Mostly moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.07,
      "end_seconds": 108.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Understood. Have you had any rash or ear pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.82,
      "end_seconds": 113.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.17,
      "end_seconds": 120.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any drooling or difficulty breathing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.9,
      "end_seconds": 124.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.37,
      "end_seconds": 127.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.34,
      "end_seconds": 132.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "that's normal as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.71,
      "end_seconds": 135.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.75,
      "end_seconds": 138.72,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "breathing's normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.1,
      "end_seconds": 161.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.99,
      "end_seconds": 166.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Trimethoprim i come out in... well, a rash"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.55,
      "end_seconds": 169.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.33,
      "end_seconds": 172.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "no surgery, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.46,
      "end_seconds": 185.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "now some background about your lifestyle"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.19,
      "end_seconds": 197.23,
      "duration_seconds": 10.04,
      "text": "I swim twice a week. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I live with my elderly mother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.32,
      "end_seconds": 203.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.73,
      "end_seconds": 208.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "No, I've always been fairly healthy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.45,
      "end_seconds": 213.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.03,
      "end_seconds": 219.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Dolo, 650 milligrams, when I get the fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.0,
      "end_seconds": 224.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.14,
      "end_seconds": 228.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.09,
      "end_seconds": 246.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "Both tonsils are red and enlarged with white patches, and the neck glands are tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.58,
      "end_seconds": 257.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "that's the examination finished. Okay, thinking it through, my working impression is tonsillitis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.58,
      "end_seconds": 300.91,
      "duration_seconds": 30.33,
      "text": "I think a throat swab makes sense here, for sore throat let's use phenoxymethylpenicillin, 500 milligrams, four times a day, for ten days you take it by mouth it's for tonsillitis gargle with warm salt water and drink plenty of fluids keep an eye out, and if you cannot swallow your saliva or have trouble breathing, call us the same day or go to emergency book a review if it isn't better in three days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.73,
      "end_seconds": 305.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "that's all from me any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.8,
      "end_seconds": 310.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "no, that's all thanks a lot"
    }
  ]
